{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Expanded the recorded file_impact from 16 to the full 26 paths changed by the merged fix (1a589bdfc2a882f09160530655f06077764b33d8 on origin/main - the only commit carrying the `rebar-ticket: 0514-92e0-e6c4-4304` trailer; the union is that single commit's change set).\n\nThe close gate rejected the previous declaration, naming 7 undeclared paths. The 10 additions are:\n\nLEGITIMATE USE - sanctioned in place with a reason-bearing `# tickets-boundary-ok` marker, behaviour unchanged (7):\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py` - the literal is the COMPARISON SUBJECT of the dir-mismatch hint; resolving it would compare the resolved tracker to itself.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py` - `_DEFAULT_TRACKER_DIR`, the absent-key default inside the reconciler's own `_resolve_tracker_dir`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` - the ConfigError-only fallback inside the read-path resolver itself.\n- `src/rebar/config.py` - the ConfigError-only default inside `tracker_dir()`, the resolver that APPLIES relocation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` - a denylist SUPERSET entry in `denied_paths()`; the configured store is appended just below, so relocation is honoured.\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` - names a dir inside the snapshot root this module creates, not the live store.\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py` - a scratch dir inside the `mkdtemp()` on the preceding line; honouring relocation here would point the throwaway view at the LIVE store.\n\nNON-BOUNDARY follow-ons (3):\n- `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py` - needs a stub for the new gate, wired into `make lint` ahead of the guard under test.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` - generated-inventory line-number refresh from the added comment blocks; no env-var semantics changed.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` - fix entry incl. the deliberate no-migration note.\n\nThe 13 genuine `config.tracker_dir()` bypasses drained by the fix remain declared across 11 files (`reconcile.py` and `__main__.py` carry two sites each); `git_adapter.py`'s `TRACKER_DIR` is declared as a LEGITIMATE USE with its value deliberately preserved as a committed-tree pathspec label.\n\nOperational note: the on-box rebar MCP server's ticket store is currently unable to push to `origin/tickets` (63 unpushed events, `final-push-rejected`/\"fetch first\" on every write), so this file_impact update was recorded through the local CLI store instead."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787890292537966001,"uuid":"275e2406-54bf-42d9-80dc-7b423aa275d5"}